KUF port (M12): the timer queue waits on a condition variable instead of spinning

The timer queue's dispatch thread waited for the next due time (or a newly queued timer) with disruptorplus's
spin_wait_strategy: short pause loops, then sched_yield, a 1 ms sleep every 20th round. That kept it at 10-15 %
of a core all the time. It now blocks on a condition variable until the next due time, and queuing a timer
wakes it (publish signals under the mutex the wait checks under, so no wake-up is lost). The strategy is a
local copy of disruptorplus's blocking_wait_strategy, whose timed wait passes the predicate before the time to
condition_variable::wait_until and does not compile. With no timer queued the wait is bounded by an hour
instead of time_point::max().

